    "compose_patient": {
      "sections": [
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.0",
          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You came to hospital with sudden drooping on the right side of your face, weakness in your right arm, and difficulty speaking. These were signs of a stroke. You had a stroke caused by a blockage in a blood vessel in the brain.\n\nYou also have atrial fibrillation (an irregular heartbeat), high blood pressure, and type 2 diabetes."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "We did a brain scan on the first day. It showed there was no bleeding, so we were able to give you a clot-busting medicine called alteplase. A second scan the next day confirmed there was no bleeding after treatment.\n\nA speech and language therapist checked your swallowing. While your swallow was not safe, we fed you through a thin tube passed through your nose. Your swallow recovered by Day 3 and the tube was removed.\n\nFrom Day 4, we started you on a blood-thinning medicine called apixaban to reduce the risk of another stroke linked to your irregular heartbeat. Your previous aspirin was stopped.\n\nThe early supported discharge team have agreed to help you continue your recovery at home."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.7",
            "sections.8"
          ],
          "text": "- The early supported discharge team will support your stroke rehabilitation in the community.\n- You have a stroke clinic appointment in 6 weeks.\n- Your GP will keep an eye on your blood pressure and your diabetes levels."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.4",
          "heading": "safety_net",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{SAFETY_NET}}"
        }
      ],
